The crucial part is the "won't forget until you move" part.  In
melee if it ever figures out where you are (no swings at your
displaced image message) it will continue to have
non-displaced combat with you until you dance.  The
advantage of displacement goes to zero if you don't know
that or you're in a situation where moving is more expensive
than continued melee combat.

Against a single monster the damage cost of a single move
is low compared to the advantage of hitting the monster until
they find you.  In a crowd it's much harder to figure out the
advantage - Yet one more reason to face a crowd one at a
time in a corridor or similar.

Until I learned this aspect of displacement I valued it a lot
less.  I still prefer robe or [oMR over displacement but I
think displacement is tied with elven until I get stealth
then I think it beats stealth - Elven boats plus displacement
doesn't suck.  Do I continue with displacement well into
the late game?  Not once I get robe or [oMR but neither
is guaranteed if I leave all of the priests alive.  I generally
don't have a pet by the time I get to the VotD so a cloak
from a priest isn't a guaranteed item for me.  Common by
the late game but not guaranteed.

